{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The export page totals were wrong because `num_pages` in `repo/paging.py` used integer floor division (`total // per_page`). That works when the row count divides evenly, but when there is a remainder it undercounts by one (e.g. 101 rows at 10 per page reported 10 pages instead of 11).\n\nThat function feeds `page_summary` in `repo/rows.py`, which is what exports use for `\"pages\"` and `last_page_start`.\n\n**Fix:** use ceiling division so a partial last page still counts:\n\n```python\nreturn (total + per_page - 1) // per_page\n```\n\nAll paging tests pass after this change."}]},"session_id":"26849a6a-6b6e-45f5-a865-d78aa41f2b54"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","duration_ms":25434,"duration_api_ms":25434,"is_error":false,"result":"Searching the codebase for how export page counts are calculated.\n\n\nThe bug is floor division in `num_pages`, which drops partial final pages. Checking tests and applying the fix.\n\n\nFixing `num_pages`: it used floor division (`//`), which omitted partial final pages.\n\n\nThe export page totals were wrong because `num_pages` in `repo/paging.py` used integer floor division (`total // per_page`). That works when the row count divides evenly, but when there is a remainder it undercounts by one (e.g. 101 rows at 10 per page reported 10 pages instead of 11).\n\nThat function feeds `page_summary` in `repo/rows.py`, which is what exports use for `\"pages\"` and `last_page_start`.\n\n**Fix:** use ceiling division so a partial last page still counts:\n\n```python\nreturn (total + per_page - 1) // per_page\n```\n\nAll paging tests pass after this change.","session_id":"26849a6a-6b6e-45f5-a865-d78aa41f2b54","request_id":"df967cf2-9a5d-4e72-9073-a5f8f37d88e1","usage":{"inputTokens":29018,"outputTokens":1233,"cacheReadTokens":93888,"cacheWriteTokens":0}}
